---
import DocsIndexLayout from '../layouts/DocsIndexLayout.astro';
import { getCollection } from 'astro:content';
import { SITE } from '../consts';

const posts = await getCollection('posts', ({ data }) => !data.draft);
const counts = {
  questions: posts.filter((p) => p.data.category === 'questions').length,
  guides: posts.filter((p) => p.data.category === 'guides').length,
  concepts: posts.filter((p) => p.data.category === 'concepts').length,
};
---
<DocsIndexLayout
  title="Start here"
  description="Where to start on mlmentorship by what you're trying to do. Curated reading paths for senior ML interviews, applied LLM work, and agent systems."
>
  <header class="head">
    <p class="kicker">Start here</p>
    <h1>Where to start, by what you're trying to do.</h1>
    <p class="lede">
      {posts.length} questions, guides, and concept notes
      can be a lot. Pick the path that matches why you're here. Each item
      links directly; come back to this page when you finish a path.
    </p>
  </header>

  <section class="sections-overview">
    <p class="sections-eyebrow">The three sections</p>
    <ul class="sections-grid">
      <li>
        <a href="/questions/">
          <h2>Questions <span class="sections-count">{counts.questions}</span></h2>
          <p>The senior ML interview canon. Each one with what L4 / L5 / L6 answers actually sound like, the tells that get a strong-hire vote, and what gets you down-leveled.</p>
          <p class="sections-when"><strong>Go here when:</strong> you have a specific question and want a level-calibrated answer.</p>
        </a>
      </li>
      <li>
        <a href="/guides/">
          <h2>Guides <span class="sections-count">{counts.guides}</span></h2>
          <p>Long-form opinion pieces on senior ML interviews, system design, and applied practice. Take a position and defend it.</p>
          <p class="sections-when"><strong>Go here when:</strong> you want a senior-IC point of view on something contested (fine-tune vs RAG, evals, inference cost).</p>
        </a>
      </li>
      <li>
        <a href="/concepts/">
          <h2>Concepts <span class="sections-count">{counts.concepts}</span></h2>
          <p>Concise notes on attention, normalization, LLM internals, optimization, and the math underneath. Each follows the same template: definition, why it matters, mechanism, common confusions.</p>
          <p class="sections-when"><strong>Go here when:</strong> you need to look up or refresh a specific concept fast.</p>
        </a>
      </li>
    </ul>
  </section>

  {SITE.features.prepTools && <section class="tools-overview" aria-labelledby="prep-tools-heading">
    <div>
      <p class="sections-eyebrow">Use what you read</p>
      <h2 id="prep-tools-heading">Turn the core library into an executable plan</h2>
      <p>Choose a workload, attempt before reading, diagnose weak dimensions, and prove improvement with spaced retrieval and simulation.</p>
    </div>
    <ul>
      <li><a href="/prep/readiness/"><strong>Readiness check</strong><span>Estimate gaps and workload</span></a></li>
      <li><a href="/prep/plans/"><strong>Prep plans</strong><span>Choose weeks and hours</span></a></li>
      <li><a href="/prep/role-paths/"><strong>Role paths</strong><span>AS, MLE, and RE sequences</span></a></li>
      <li><a href="/prep/frontier-labs/"><strong>Frontier labs</strong><span>Verify current round formats</span></a></li>
      <li><a href="/prep/labs/"><strong>Executable labs</strong><span>Practice realistic work samples</span></a></li>
      <li><a href="/prep/practice/"><strong>Practice method</strong><span>Attempt, diagnose, retry</span></a></li>
      <li><a href="/prep/simulations/"><strong>Simulations</strong><span>Test the integrated loop</span></a></li>
    </ul>
  </section>}

    <section class="path" id="preparing-for-a-senior-ml-interview-loop">
      <header>
        <h2>1. Preparing for a senior ML interview loop</h2>
        <p>You have a loop in 2-8 weeks. You want to know what's actually tested at L5/L6 vs. what showed up on your old prep material.</p>
      </header>
      <ol>
        {SITE.features.prepTools && <li>Start with the <a href="/prep/readiness/">private readiness check</a>, then choose an <a href="/prep/plans/">hours-based 2-, 4-, or 8-week plan</a></li>}
        {SITE.features.prepTools && <li>Use the <a href="/prep/practice/">round-specific practice method</a> on every question</li>}
        {SITE.features.prepTools && <li>If you are interviewing at a frontier lab, verify the <a href="/prep/frontier-labs/">current format evidence</a> and substitute only the matching <a href="/prep/labs/">work sample</a></li>}
        <li><a href="/guides/five-things-as-interview-tests/">The 5 things AS interviews test for</a></li>
        <li><a href="/guides/l5-vs-l6-faang-ml/">L5 vs L6 calibration: what's the difference</a></li>
        <li><a href="/questions/most-ambitious-project/">Tell me about your most ambitious project</a></li>
        <li><a href="/questions/how-would-you-evaluate-an-llm-application/">How would you evaluate an LLM application</a></li>
        <li><a href="/questions/reduce-llm-inference-cost-10x/">Reduce LLM inference cost 10x</a></li>
        <li>Browse <a href="/questions/">all {counts.questions} questions</a></li>
      </ol>
    </section>

    <section class="path" id="shipping-an-llm-product-right-now">
      <header>
        <h2>2. Shipping LLM products or building agents</h2>
        <p>You're building a real LLM application or agent system. mlmentorship is interview-focused; my opinion writing on applied LLMs and agents lives on my personal site.</p>
      </header>
      <ol>
        <li>Browse essays at <a href="https://hsaghir.com/blog/" rel="noopener">hsaghir.com/blog</a> (verification asymmetry, similarity-is-all-you-need, the-loop-is-the-product, under-specified coding agents).</li>
        <li>Skim <a href="https://github.com/hsaghir/looplet" rel="noopener">Looplet</a>, my iterator-first agent framework.</li>
        <li>For consulting on agents/evals/post-training: <a href="https://hsaghir.com/work-together/" rel="noopener">hsaghir.com/work-together</a>.</li>
      </ol>
    </section>

    <section class="path" id="phd-or-postdoc-transitioning-to-industry">
      <header>
        <h2>3. PhD or postdoc transitioning to industry</h2>
        <p>You have research credentials. You want to know what industry interviews look like and how research projects translate to "ambitious project" stories.</p>
      </header>
      <ol>
        <li><a href="/guides/as-vs-mle-vs-re/">Applied Scientist vs MLE vs Research Engineer</a></li>
        <li><a href="/guides/five-things-as-interview-tests/">The 5 things AS interviews test for</a></li>
        <li><a href="/questions/most-ambitious-project/">Tell me about your most ambitious project</a></li>
        <li><a href="/questions/disagreed-with-senior/">When you disagreed with a senior person</a></li>
        <li><a href="/questions/scope-ambiguous-problem/">Scoping an ambiguous problem</a></li>
      </ol>
    </section>

    <section class="path" id="building-deep-technical-foundations">
      <header>
        <h2>4. Building deep technical foundations</h2>
        <p>You want the canonical ML/DL reference, organized so you can study for breadth and depth in parallel.</p>
      </header>
      <ol>
        <li>Foundations: <a href="/concepts/matrices-as-linear-maps/">matrices as linear maps</a> → <a href="/concepts/svd-and-pca/">SVD and PCA</a> → <a href="/concepts/eigenvalues-and-spectral-theorem/">eigenvalues</a></li>
        <li>Probability: <a href="/concepts/maximum-likelihood-estimation/">MLE</a> → <a href="/concepts/kl-divergence/">KL divergence</a> → <a href="/concepts/bayes-rule-and-posterior/">Bayes rule</a></li>
        <li>Deep learning: <a href="/concepts/backpropagation/">backprop</a> → <a href="/concepts/attention-mechanism/">attention</a> → <a href="/concepts/transformer-architecture/">transformers</a></li>
        <li>LLM internals: <a href="/concepts/flashattention/">FlashAttention</a> → <a href="/concepts/kv-cache/">KV cache</a> → <a href="/concepts/speculative-decoding/">speculative decoding</a></li>
        <li>Browse <a href="/concepts/">all {counts.concepts} concepts</a> by sub-category</li>
      </ol>
    </section>

    <section class="path" id="engineering-leader-hiring-manager">
      <header>
        <h2>5. Engineering leader / hiring manager</h2>
        <p>You're not preparing for an interview. You want to calibrate what good looks like, what to test for, or who to hire.</p>
      </header>
      <ol>
        <li><a href="/guides/five-things-as-interview-tests/">What senior ML interviews actually test</a></li>
        <li><a href="/guides/l5-vs-l6-faang-ml/">L5 vs L6 calibration</a></li>
        <li><a href="/guides/as-vs-mle-vs-re/">AS vs MLE vs Research Engineer (which role to hire)</a></li>
        <li><a href="/guides/llm-evals-the-hardest-part/">Why your team's eval pipeline is probably broken</a></li>
        <li><a href="https://hsaghir.com/work-together/" rel="noopener">If you'd like a senior sounding board on a specific decision</a></li>
      </ol>
    </section>

    <p class="closer">
      Lost? Press <kbd>/</kbd> to search. Or browse the three sections from the top
      nav: <a href="/questions/">Questions</a>, <a href="/guides/">Guides</a>,
      <a href="/concepts/">Concepts</a>.
    </p>
  </DocsIndexLayout>

<style>
  .head {
    margin-bottom: 2rem;
    max-width: 42rem;
  }
  .head h1 {
    font-family: var(--font-display);
    font-weight: 700;
    font-size: clamp(1.6rem, 4vw, 2.2rem);
    line-height: 1.15;
    letter-spacing: -0.02em;
    margin: 0 0 1rem;
  }
  .kicker {
    font-family: var(--font-mono);
    font-size: 0.74rem;
    text-transform: uppercase;
    letter-spacing: 0.14em;
    color: var(--c-accent);
    margin: 0 0 1rem;
  }
  .lede {
    font-size: 1.1rem;
    color: var(--c-text-soft);
    margin-bottom: 2.5rem;
  }

  .tools-overview {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: minmax(0, 1.1fr) minmax(18rem, 1fr);
    gap: 1.5rem;
    margin: 0 0 2.5rem;
    padding: 1.3rem;
    border: 1px solid var(--c-rule);
    border-radius: var(--radius-lg);
    background: var(--c-bg-tint);
  }
  .tools-overview h2 { margin: 0 0 .5rem; font-size: 1.25rem; }
  .tools-overview > div > p:last-child { margin: 0; color: var(--c-text-soft); font-size: .9rem; }
  .tools-overview ul { display: grid; grid-template-columns: repeat(2, minmax(0, 1fr)); gap: .45rem; list-style: none; padding: 0; margin: 0; }
  .tools-overview a { display: block; height: 100%; padding: .65rem .7rem; border: 1px solid var(--c-rule); border-radius: var(--radius); background: var(--c-surface); color: inherit; text-decoration: none; }
  .tools-overview a:hover { border-color: var(--c-accent); }
  .tools-overview strong, .tools-overview span { display: block; }
  .tools-overview strong { font-size: .82rem; }
  .tools-overview span { color: var(--c-muted); font-size: .72rem; }
  @media (max-width: 700px) {
    .tools-overview { grid-template-columns: 1fr; }
    .tools-overview ul { grid-template-columns: 1fr; }
  }

  /* The three sections overview */
  .sections-overview {
    margin: 0 0 3rem;
    padding: 0 0 2rem;
    border-bottom: 1px solid var(--c-rule);
  }
  .sections-eyebrow {
    font-family: var(--font-mono);
    font-size: 0.72rem;
    text-transform: uppercase;
    letter-spacing: 0.16em;
    color: var(--c-muted);
    margin: 0 0 1rem;
  }
  .sections-grid {
    list-style: none;
    padding: 0;
    margin: 0;
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: repeat(auto-fit, minmax(15rem, 1fr));
    gap: 1rem;
  }
  .sections-grid > li { margin: 0; padding: 0; }
  .sections-grid a {
    display: block;
    padding: 1.2rem 1.3rem 1.4rem;
    background: var(--c-surface);
    border: 1px solid var(--c-rule);
    border-radius: var(--radius-lg);
    text-decoration: none;
    color: inherit;
    transition: border-color var(--transition), transform var(--transition);
  }
  .sections-grid a:hover {
    border-color: var(--c-accent);
    transform: translateY(-2px);
  }
  .sections-grid h2 {
    font-family: var(--font-display);
    font-size: 1.1rem;
    font-weight: 600;
    color: var(--c-text);
    margin: 0 0 0.6rem;
    letter-spacing: -0.01em;
    display: flex;
    align-items: baseline;
    gap: 0.5rem;
  }
  .sections-count {
    font-family: var(--font-mono);
    font-size: 0.78rem;
    color: var(--c-accent);
    font-weight: 500;
  }
  .sections-grid p {
    font-size: 0.92rem;
    line-height: 1.55;
    color: var(--c-text-soft);
    margin: 0 0 0.6rem;
  }
  .sections-when {
    font-size: 0.85rem;
    color: var(--c-muted);
    margin: 0.8rem 0 0;
  }
  .sections-when strong {
    color: var(--c-text-soft);
    font-weight: 600;
  }

  .path {
    margin-bottom: 2.5rem;
    padding-bottom: 2rem;
    border-bottom: 1px solid var(--c-rule-soft);
  }
  .path:last-of-type { border-bottom: 0; }
  .path header h2 {
    font-size: 1.2rem;
    font-weight: 600;
    margin: 0 0 0.4rem;
    color: var(--c-text);
  }
  .path header p {
    color: var(--c-text-soft);
    font-size: 0.95rem;
    margin: 0 0 1rem;
  }
  .path ol {
    padding-left: 1.4rem;
    color: var(--c-text-soft);
  }
  .path ol li { margin: 0.4rem 0; }
  .path ol a { color: var(--c-link); }
  .closer {
    margin-top: 3rem;
    color: var(--c-muted);
    font-size: 0.95rem;
  }
  .closer kbd {
    font-family: var(--font-mono);
    background: var(--c-kbd-bg);
    border: 1px solid var(--c-rule);
    padding: 0.05rem 0.4rem;
    border-radius: 4px;
    font-size: 0.85em;
  }
</style>
